WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.562
How expressive is a graph neural network?

00:00:02.642 --> 00:00:07.395
For years the field has answered that with the
Weisfeiler-Lehman hierarchy,

00:00:07.475 --> 00:00:12.551
and the gold standard has been to design a model
and then prove it matches, say,

00:00:12.631 --> 00:00:13.904
the third-order test.

00:00:13.984 --> 00:00:18.093
But that proof comes after the design, almost as an
afterthought.

00:00:18.173 --> 00:00:24.086
What has been missing is a systematic way to go the
other direction: to start from a language

00:00:24.166 --> 00:00:27.179
we already know is exactly as powerful as 3-W-L,

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:30.917
and mechanically build a network that inherits that power.

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:36.330
Without such a recipe, every expressive
architecture is a fresh, hand-crafted proof.
